# deploy
NODE_ENV - runtime mode of the wallet gateway process, production on the platform
PORT - port the wallet gateway listens on behind the platform proxy
ATTESTOR_NODE_KEY - platform secret holding this attestor's node key, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_NODE_KEY_FILE
ATTESTOR_BACKUP_KEY - platform secret holding this attestor's backup key, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_BACKUP_KEY_FILE
ATTESTOR_TLS_CERT - platform secret holding this attestor's TLS certificate, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_TLS_CERT_FILE
ATTESTOR_TLS_KEY - platform secret holding this attestor's TLS private key, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_TLS_KEY_FILE
ATTESTOR_TLS_CA - platform secret holding the CA bundle for peers and the gateway, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_TLS_CA_FILE
ATTESTOR_OPERATOR_CA - platform secret holding the operator CA bundle, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_OPERATOR_CA_FILE
ATTESTOR_REPLICA_KEY - platform secret holding this attestor's own OpenSSH private key for the snapshot replica, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_REPLICA_KEY_FILE; set it before the next attestor deploy, because the platform destroys a machine whose file mapping names an unset secret
ATTESTOR_REPLICA_HOST_KEY - platform secret holding the replica server's SSH host public key as one OpenSSH public key line, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_REPLICA_HOST_KEY_FILE; set it before the next attestor deploy, because the platform destroys a machine whose file mapping names an unset secret
ATTESTOR_REPLICA_ADDR - platform secret holding the replica server's SSH host:port, read as an environment variable and named nowhere else
ATTESTOR_REPLICA_USER - platform secret holding the replica's dedicated backup user, which the replica gives an SFTP-only login chrooted to the replica directory, one authorised key per attestor and no shell or forwarding
LAYERX_GATEWAY_LISTEN - socket address the shared endpoint listens on, defaulting to all interfaces on port 9443
LAYERX_GATEWAY_NETWORK_ID - network identifier the shared endpoint expects from its kernel backends, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_PROTOCOL_NETWORK_ID - numeric protocol network identifier of the kernel, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_LXP_WIRE_VERSION - LXP wire version the shared endpoint speaks
LAYERX_GATEWAY_IDEMPOTENCY_SECONDS - retention of idempotency records in seconds
LAYERX_GATEWAY_CAPABILITIES_TTL_SECONDS - cache lifetime of the capabilities answer in seconds
LAYERX_GATEWAY_LISTENER - listener mode of the shared endpoint: tls, the default, terminates TLS with the certificate and key; plain serves plain HTTP behind the platform proxy and refuses both of them
LAYERX_GATEWAY_TLS_CERT_DER - path to the shared endpoint's DER server certificate
LAYERX_GATEWAY_TLS_KEY_DER - path to the shared endpoint's DER PKCS8 server key
LAYERX_GATEWAY_OUTBOUND_CA_DER - path to the DER CA that authenticates the endpoint's upstream services
LAYERX_GATEWAY_CLIENT_IDENTITY_PKCS12 - path to the PKCS12 client identity the endpoint presents upstream
LAYERX_GATEWAY_CLIENT_IDENTITY_PASSWORD_FILE - path to the password of the PKCS12 client identity
LAYERX_GATEWAY_COMPONENT_URL - agent boundary base URL, the kernel app's .internal name on 9446 in human/wallet/deploy/endpoint.toml
LAYERX_GATEWAY_COMPONENT_TOKEN_FILE - path to the agent boundary bearer token
LAYERX_GATEWAY_AUTHORITY_URL - receipt authority base URL, the kernel app's .internal name on 9445 in human/wallet/deploy/endpoint.toml
LAYERX_GATEWAY_AUTHORITY_TOKEN_FILE - path to the receipt authority bearer token
LAYERX_GATEWAY_IDENTITY_URL - identity service base URL, the identity app's .internal name on 9443 in human/wallet/deploy/endpoint.toml
LAYERX_GATEWAY_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE - path to the identity service bearer token
LAYERX_GATEWAY_IDENTITY_PROVISIONING_TOKEN_FILE - path to the identity provisioning token used by registration
LAYERX_GATEWAY_PROGRAM_REGISTRY_URL - program registry base URL, the registry app's .internal name on 9420 in human/wallet/deploy/endpoint.toml; configured_kernel requires it in kernel mode
LAYERX_GATEWAY_PROGRAM_REGISTRY_TOKEN_FILE - path to the program registry bearer token
LAYERX_GATEWAY_PUBLIC_CORE_URL - public core read base URL, the kernel app's .internal name on 9443 in human/wallet/deploy/endpoint.toml; px_getNetwork reports kernel.available only when it is set
LAYERX_GATEWAY_PAXEER_RPC_URLS - JSON array of two to eight chain RPC https urls tried in order for eth_ relay, optional, set as a Fly secret of the endpoint app to two serving RPC names of tools/bringup/search-front.sh names
LAYERX_GATEWAY_INDEXER_URL - indexer base URL for unified history, optional, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_FAUCET_URL - faucet service base URL, optional, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_FAUCET_SERVICE_TOKEN_FILE - path to the faucet service token
LAYERX_GATEWAY_REDIS_URL - Redis URL of the endpoint's shared store, rediss:// at the Redis app's .internal name, set as a platform secret
LAYERX_GATEWAY_REDIS_USERNAME_FILE - path to the Redis username
LAYERX_GATEWAY_REDIS_PASSWORD_FILE - path to the Redis password
LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_PUBLIC_KEY_FILE - path to the trusted sequencer public key
LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_ID_FILE - path to the trusted sequencer identifier
LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_FIRST_BATCH_FILE - path to the first batch the sequencer authorisation covers
LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_LAST_BATCH_FILE - path to the last batch the sequencer authorisation covers
LAYERX_GATEWAY_KEY_PROVISIONING_KEY_FILE - path to the 64-hex key provisioning key
LAYERX_GATEWAY_MODULE_REGISTRY_FILE - path to the module registry JSON document
ENDPOINT_OUTBOUND_CA - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_OUTBOUND_CA_DER
ENDPOINT_CLIENT_CERT - platform secret holding the PEM client certificate of the gateway-client row of tools/bringup/ca.sh, mounted for its expiry check
ENDPOINT_CLIENT_P12 - platform secret from the gateway-client row of tools/bringup/ca.sh written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_CLIENT_IDENTITY_PKCS12
ENDPOINT_CLIENT_PASSWORD - platform secret from the gateway-client row of tools/bringup/ca.sh written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_CLIENT_IDENTITY_PASSWORD_FILE
ENDPOINT_COMPONENT_TOKEN - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_COMPONENT_TOKEN_FILE
ENDPOINT_AUTHORITY_TOKEN - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_AUTHORITY_TOKEN_FILE
ENDPOINT_IDENTITY_TOKEN - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE
ENDPOINT_IDENTITY_PROVISIONING_TOKEN - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_IDENTITY_PROVISIONING_TOKEN_FILE
ENDPOINT_PROGRAM_REGISTRY_TOKEN - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_PROGRAM_REGISTRY_TOKEN_FILE
ENDPOINT_FAUCET_SERVICE_TOKEN - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_FAUCET_SERVICE_TOKEN_FILE
ENDPOINT_REDIS_USERNAME - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_REDIS_USERNAME_FILE
ENDPOINT_REDIS_PASSWORD - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_REDIS_PASSWORD_FILE
ENDPOINT_SEQUENCER_PUBLIC_KEY - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_PUBLIC_KEY_FILE
ENDPOINT_SEQUENCER_ID - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_ID_FILE
ENDPOINT_SEQUENCER_FIRST_BATCH - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_FIRST_BATCH_FILE
ENDPOINT_SEQUENCER_LAST_BATCH - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_SEQUENCER_LAST_BATCH_FILE
ENDPOINT_KEY_PROVISIONING_KEY - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_KEY_PROVISIONING_KEY_FILE
ENDPOINT_MODULE_REGISTRY - platform secret written to the file named by LAYERX_GATEWAY_MODULE_REGISTRY_FILE
REDIS_CONF - platform secret holding the private Redis server configuration, written to /run/secrets/redis.conf
REDIS_TLS_CERT - platform secret holding the private Redis server's PEM certificate, signed by the CA in ENDPOINT_OUTBOUND_CA, written to /run/secrets/redis.crt
REDIS_TLS_KEY - platform secret holding the private Redis server's PEM private key, written to /run/secrets/redis.key
REDIS_TLS_CA - platform secret holding the PEM form of the CA in ENDPOINT_OUTBOUND_CA, written to /run/secrets/ca.crt
REDIS_ACL - platform secret holding the private Redis ACL file with the default user off and the endpoint's user, written to /run/secrets/users.acl
# attestor
ATTESTOR_NODE_ID - identifier of this attestor node within the participant set
ATTESTOR_REGION - region label this node reports in health
ATTESTOR_LISTEN_ADDR - host:port the attestor API listens on
ATTESTOR_PEER_LISTEN_ADDR - host:port the peer transport listens on
ATTESTOR_PEERS - comma-separated id=host:port list of the other attestor nodes
ATTESTOR_PEER_PINS - comma-separated id=sha256 list pinning each peer's TLS public key, 64 hex characters per pin, set as a platform secret
ATTESTOR_NODE_KEY_FILE - path to the node key file (32 raw bytes or 64 hex characters) that encrypts the share store
ATTESTOR_DATA_DIR - directory holding the encrypted share store
ATTESTOR_CEREMONY - true enables keys.import for the operator during a ceremony window
ATTESTOR_CHAIN_ID - EVM chain id every decoded transaction is pinned to
ATTESTOR_JWKS_URL - identity provider JWKS endpoint used to verify user tokens
ATTESTOR_JWT_ISSUER - expected issuer of user tokens
ATTESTOR_JWT_AUDIENCE - expected audience of user tokens
ATTESTOR_POLICY_FILE - path to the default signing policy
ATTESTOR_TLS_CERT_FILE - path to this node's TLS certificate
ATTESTOR_TLS_KEY_FILE - path to this node's TLS private key
ATTESTOR_TLS_CA_FILE - path to the CA bundle that authenticates peers and the gateway; API clients chaining to it may call keys.generate and sign only
ATTESTOR_OPERATOR_CA_FILE - path to the CA bundle that authenticates the operator identity; API clients chaining to it may call keys.import, keys.refresh and keys.addshare only; must be a different CA from ATTESTOR_TLS_CA_FILE
ATTESTOR_BACKUP_KEY_FILE - path to the key file (32 raw bytes or 64 hex characters) that encrypts store snapshots
ATTESTOR_BACKUP_DIR - directory where encrypted store snapshots are written
ATTESTOR_SNAPSHOT_INTERVAL - duration between scheduled snapshots into ATTESTOR_BACKUP_DIR, at least 1s, default 1h; a snapshot also follows every successful keys.generate, keys.import, keys.refresh and keys.addshare
ATTESTOR_SNAPSHOT_RETAIN - number of newest snapshots kept, at least 1, default 48; with a replica configured an older snapshot is deleted only once replica-ledger.json records it as shipped with the same size and digest
ATTESTOR_REPLICA_KEY_FILE - path to this attestor's OpenSSH private key for the replica; setting any ATTESTOR_REPLICA_ variable requires all six
ATTESTOR_REPLICA_HOST_KEY_FILE - path to the replica's expected SSH host public key; any other host key is refused and nothing is uploaded
ATTESTOR_REPLICA_REMOTE_DIR - absolute per-node directory inside the replica user's chroot, /attestor-<node id>, created by the operator on the replica and writable by that user
ATTESTOR_REPLICA_INTERVAL - duration between shipping passes over ATTESTOR_BACKUP_DIR, at least 1s; each snapshot is uploaded once, verified by size and digest and recorded in replica-ledger.json under ATTESTOR_DATA_DIR
ATTESTOR_RPC_URL - chain RPC endpoint used to read nonces and binding state
ATTESTOR_JWT_MAX_AGE - Go duration a user token stays usable after its issue time (default 1h); a token authorises any number of distinct signing requests until then, and each node records the token and request digest in the share store and refuses the identical request under the same token
ATTESTOR_AGENTS_FILE - path to the JSON list of registered agent principals (public_key hex, frozen, key_ids); unset refuses agent requests with token_unavailable
ATTESTOR_AGENT_MAX_EXPIRY - Go duration an agent request's expiry may lie ahead of the node clock (default 5m); agent nonces are recorded in the share store
ATTESTOR_KERNEL_POLICY_FILE - path to the kernel policy for lx_activity, lx_bind and lx_grant; needs ATTESTOR_RPC_URL; unset refuses every kernel kind with no_policy
ATTESTOR_ACTIVITY_TYPES - comma-separated kernel activity types (module << 16 | operation, decimal or 0x hex) the daemon decodes for lx_activity; a type left out is refused as a decode error before any policy runs

# gateway
NODE_ENV - runtime mode of the gateway: development, test or production
PORT - TCP port the gateway HTTP server listens on
LOG_LEVEL - gateway log verbosity
CORS_ORIGINS - comma-separated browser origins allowed to call the gateway, with single-level wildcard subdomains
SUPABASE_URL - Supabase project URL whose published JWKS verifies user access tokens
DATABASE_URL - connection string of the gateway's wallet database
DATABASE_POOL_MAX - maximum connections in the gateway's database pool
WALLET_MASTER_KEY - base64 32-byte key that encrypts legacy wallet key envelopes at rest
WALLET_MASTER_KEY_VERSION - version number of the active wallet master key
HYPERPAXEER_CHAIN_ID - EVM chain id the gateway signs for
HYPERPAXEER_RPC_URL - EVM JSON-RPC endpoint used for reads and broadcasts, the router URL https://api-mainnet-beta.paxeer.network set as a Fly secret of the wallet gateway app
HYPERPAXEER_EXPLORER_URL - block explorer base URL returned to clients for transaction links
POLICY_MAX_TX_VALUE_WEI - per-transaction native value cap for standard wallets
POLICY_MAX_DAILY_VALUE_WEI - rolling daily native value cap for standard wallets
POLICY_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE - signing requests allowed per wallet per minute
FUNDED_TREASURY_PRIVATE_KEY - treasury signing key of the funded lane, disabled when unset
FUNDED_USDL_ADDRESS - USDL token contract used as funded-lane collateral
FUNDED_USDL_DECIMALS - decimals of the USDL token
FUNDED_GAS_REFILL_THRESHOLD_WEI - native balance below which a funded wallet is topped up
FUNDED_GAS_REFILL_AMOUNT_WEI - native amount sent per funded-wallet top-up
FUNDED_EVALUATOR_INTERVAL_MS - tick interval of the funded drawdown evaluator
PAXSCAN_API_URL - explorer API base used to value funded wallets
PAXSCAN_TIMEOUT_MS - timeout of one explorer API request
PAXSCAN_CACHE_TTL_MS - lifetime of cached explorer valuations
FUNDED_BALANCE_READ_QUORUM - number of RPC reads sampled per funded balance read
FUNDED_DAILY_RESET_UTC_HOUR - UTC hour at which the funded daily drawdown window resets
API_WORKERS - number of gateway worker processes
AGENT_JWT_SECRET - HS256 secret that signs gateway-minted agent tokens, agent lane disabled when unset
AGENT_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS - lifetime of an agent token
AGENT_CHALLENGE_TTL_SECONDS - lifetime of an agent authentication challenge
AGENT_DEFAULT_FROZEN - whether a newly seen agent principal starts frozen
AGENT_DEFAULT_MODE - initial mode of a newly seen agent principal
AGENT_BIND_OWNER_FROM_DID - whether an agent is bound to the owner named in its DID label
AGENT_DEFAULT_MAX_TX_VALUE_WEI - default per-transaction native value cap for agent wallets
AGENT_DEFAULT_MAX_DAILY_VALUE_WEI - default rolling daily native value cap for agent wallets
AGENT_DEFAULT_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE - default signing requests per agent per minute
AGENT_DEFAULT_MAX_APPROVE_WEI - default cap on ERC-20 approval amounts for agent wallets
LAYERX_VAULT_ADDRESS - LayerX custody vault contract targeted by agent deposit actions
LAYER_X_DB_URI - read-only connection string of the LayerX sequencer database
ACTION_CONFIRMATIONS - block confirmations before an agent action transaction is final
ACTION_RECEIPT_TIMEOUT_MS - maximum wait for one agent action receipt
ACTION_WORKER_INTERVAL_MS - tick interval of the agent action worker
ACTION_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_MS - sweep interval of the agent action reconciler
ACTION_FEE_BUMP_PERCENT - fee increase applied when replacing a stuck agent action transaction
LAYERX_SYNC_INTERVAL_MS - interval of the LayerX mirror sync worker
NEXT_PUBLIC_PAXEER_WALLET_API - wallet gateway base URL used by the demo
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL - Supabase project URL used by the demo for sign-in
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY - Supabase publishable key used by the demo for sign-in
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_REDIRECT_URL - sign-in callback URL of the demo
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL - public origin of the demo used for page metadata
NEXT_PUBLIC_PAXEER_ATTESTOR_URL - attestor base URL the wallet app service worker treats as network-only; unset when browsers never reach the attestors
CHECK_LIVE_GATEWAY_BASE - base URL of a deployed wallet gateway checked by tools/wallet/check-live.sh gateway
CHECK_LIVE_GATEWAY_TOKEN - access token of a provisioned test identity that tools/wallet/check-live.sh gateway reads /v1/wallet/me with
NEXT_PUBLIC_PAXEER_HUMAN_API - human service base URL the wallet app plans and submits intents against, https://api-hull.paxeer.network on the paxport service
CHECK_LIVE_HUMAN_BASE - base URL of a deployed human service checked by tools/wallet/check-live.sh human and human-session
CHECK_LIVE_HUMAN_ORIGIN - https origin of the wallet app that tools/wallet/check-live.sh human and human-session call the human service from
CHECK_LIVE_HUMAN_ASSERTION - wallet identity assertion of a provisioned, funded test identity that tools/wallet/check-live.sh human-session sends as the plan's bearer
CHECK_LIVE_HUMAN_ASSET - 64-hex asset id of the kernel's native asset that tools/wallet/check-live.sh human-session plans the golden intent in
CHECK_LIVE_HUMAN_DESTINATION - kernel account the golden intent of tools/wallet/check-live.sh human-session pays
# gateway
ATTESTOR_ENDPOINTS - comma-separated https base URLs of the five attestor nodes the gateway signs through
ATTESTOR_CLIENT_CERT_FILE - path to the gateway's mutual TLS client certificate presented to the attestors
ATTESTOR_CLIENT_KEY_FILE - path to the private key of the gateway's mutual TLS client certificate
SPONSOR_PRIVATE_KEY - platform secret holding the account setup sponsor key, written to the file named by SPONSOR_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE
SPONSOR_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE - path to the 64-hex private key of the account that tops up binding gas for new unified accounts
ACCOUNT_SETUP_GAS_CAP_WEI - largest binding gas top-up in wei the sponsor pays for one account
ATTESTOR_CA_FILE - path to the CA bundle that authenticates the attestor nodes
ATTESTOR_CLIENT_CERT - platform secret holding the gateway's attestor client certificate, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_CLIENT_CERT_FILE
ATTESTOR_CLIENT_KEY - platform secret holding the private key of the gateway's attestor client certificate, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_CLIENT_KEY_FILE
ATTESTOR_CA - platform secret holding the CA bundle that authenticates the attestor nodes, written to the file named by ATTESTOR_CA_FILE
ATTESTOR_QUORUM - number of healthy attestors a signing session needs, defaulting to 3
ATTESTOR_HEALTH_INTERVAL_MS - interval between attestor health probes in milliseconds, defaulting to 5000
ATTESTOR_TIMEOUT_MS - timeout of one attestor request in milliseconds, defaulting to 15000
RPC_URLS - comma-separated chain RPC URLs of the gateway's RPC pool, defaulting to the sixteen public mainnet hosts; set as a Fly secret of the wallet gateway app to the router URL followed by the serving RPC names
RPC_LAG_THRESHOLD_BLOCKS - blocks an RPC endpoint may trail the best head before it leaves the pool, defaulting to 20
RPC_HEALTH_INTERVAL_MS - interval between RPC pool health checks in milliseconds, defaulting to 5000
RPC_TIMEOUT_MS - timeout of one RPC request in milliseconds, defaulting to 8000
RATE_LIMIT_CLIENT_PER_MINUTE - signing requests one bearer subject may make per minute, defaulting to 120
RATE_LIMIT_ACCOUNT_PER_MINUTE - signing requests one wallet account may receive per minute, defaulting to 60
AGENT_JWT_SECRET - platform secret signing the read-scoped agent token; unset disables the agent lane
AGENT_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS - lifetime of the read-scoped agent token in seconds
AGENT_CHALLENGE_TTL_SECONDS - lifetime of an agent authentication challenge in seconds
AGENT_REQUEST_MAX_TTL_SECONDS - furthest expiry in seconds an agent request signature or claim counter-signature may carry, default 300
LAYERX_USDL_ADDRESS - USDL token address used by the kernel deposit action
LAYERX_USDL_DECIMALS - USDL token decimals used when the token does not report them
FUNDED_TREASURY_PRIVATE_KEY - removed with the funded lane; must not be set anywhere
FUNDED_USDL_ADDRESS - removed; replaced by LAYERX_USDL_ADDRESS
FUNDED_USDL_DECIMALS - removed; replaced by LAYERX_USDL_DECIMALS
FUNDED_GAS_REFILL_THRESHOLD_WEI - removed with the funded lane
FUNDED_GAS_REFILL_AMOUNT_WEI - removed with the funded lane
FUNDED_EVALUATOR_INTERVAL_MS - removed with the funded lane
FUNDED_BALANCE_READ_QUORUM - removed with the funded lane
FUNDED_DAILY_RESET_UTC_HOUR - removed with the funded lane
PAXSCAN_API_URL - removed with the funded lane
PAXSCAN_TIMEOUT_MS - removed with the funded lane
PAXSCAN_CACHE_TTL_MS - removed with the funded lane
AGENT_BIND_OWNER_FROM_DID - removed; an owner is recorded only through the authenticated claim route
# human service
LAYERX_HUMAN_ATTESTOR_NODES - comma-separated id=address list of the attestors that hold human custody keys; when unset the human service keeps the remote KMS
LAYERX_HUMAN_ATTESTOR_SIGNERS - comma-separated ids of at least three configured attestors that form the signing quorum
LAYERX_HUMAN_ATTESTOR_ROOT_CERTIFICATE_DER - path to the DER CA that authenticates the attestors
LAYERX_HUMAN_ATTESTOR_CLIENT_CERTIFICATE_DER - path to the DER client certificate, issued by the CA in ATTESTOR_TLS_CA_FILE, that the human service presents to the attestors for keys.generate and sign
LAYERX_HUMAN_ATTESTOR_CLIENT_PRIVATE_KEY_DER - path to the DER PKCS8 private key of the client certificate
LAYERX_HUMAN_ATTESTOR_DEADLINE_SECONDS - deadline in seconds for each attestor request; startup is refused when a signing attestor is unreachable
LAYERX_HUMAN_LISTENER - plain when the platform proxy terminates public TLS and forwards plain HTTP to the service, unset or tls to terminate TLS in the service; plain refuses the two TLS paths below by name
LAYERX_HUMAN_BIND - socket address the human service listens on; behind the platform proxy its port is the http_service internal port
LAYERX_HUMAN_TLS_CERT_DER - path to the DER certificate the service presents in tls mode; must be unset in plain mode
LAYERX_HUMAN_TLS_KEY_DER - path to the DER private key of that certificate; must be unset in plain mode
LAYERX_HUMAN_COMPONENT_SOCKET - absolute path of the unix socket where layerx-human-components serves the business operations; readiness reports unavailable while nothing listens there
LAYERX_HUMAN_WEB_ORIGIN - comma-separated https origins of the wallet app that may call mutating operations and receive the browser preflight answer
LAYERX_HUMAN_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE - requests one principal or bootstrap address may make per minute before rate-limited
LAYERX_HUMAN_MAX_PRINCIPALS - number of principals tracked by the rate limiter before the oldest is evicted
LAYERX_HUMAN_MAX_HEADER_BYTES - largest request head the service reads before answering invalid-request
LAYERX_HUMAN_MAX_BODY_BYTES - largest JSON body the service reads before answering invalid-request
LAYERX_HUMAN_MAX_CONNECTIONS - concurrent connections the listener admits; further connections are dropped
LAYERX_HUMAN_IO_DEADLINE_SECONDS - read and write deadline of one connection in seconds
LAYERX_HUMAN_COMPONENT_ALLOWED_UID - uid that may connect to the components socket; must equal the uid of the components process
LAYERX_HUMAN_COMPONENT_WORKERS - worker threads of the components server
LAYERX_HUMAN_COMPONENT_QUEUE_CAPACITY - queued requests the components server holds before refusing
LAYERX_HUMAN_RECIPIENT_SOCKET - path of the notification recipient socket the components server calls
LAYERX_HUMAN_RECIPIENT_CALLER_UID - uid the recipient socket must present
LAYERX_HUMAN_RECIPIENT_CALLER_GID - gid the recipient socket must present
LAYERX_HUMAN_RECIPIENT_DEADLINE_SECONDS - deadline of one recipient call in seconds
LAYERX_HUMAN_MAINTENANCE_INTERVAL_SECONDS - seconds between two maintenance passes over journeys, notifications and retention
LAYERX_HUMAN_MAINTENANCE_MAXIMUM_ITEMS - items one maintenance pass handles
LAYERX_HUMAN_STORE_ROOT - absolute directory of the principal, journey, audit and telemetry stores
LAYERX_HUMAN_CUSTODY_ROOT - absolute directory of the custody keystore
LAYERX_HUMAN_AUTH_INDEX_ROOT - absolute directory of the authentication index
LAYERX_HUMAN_TENANCY_DIGEST - base64url 32-byte key that scopes tenancy digests
LAYERX_HUMAN_AUTH_INDEX_KEY - base64url 32-byte MAC key of the authentication index
LAYERX_HUMAN_STREAM_CURSOR_KEY - base64url 32-byte key that authenticates stream cursors
LAYERX_HUMAN_CAPABILITY_TTL_SECONDS - lifetime of an issued capability, between one and sixty seconds
LAYERX_HUMAN_AGENT - prefix of the agent daemon transport limits below
LAYERX_HUMAN_AGENT_SOCKET - absolute path of the agent daemon socket
LAYERX_HUMAN_AGENT_MAX_FRAME_BYTES - largest frame exchanged with the agent daemon
LAYERX_HUMAN_AGENT_MAX_CONNECTIONS - concurrent connections to the agent daemon
LAYERX_HUMAN_AGENT_MAX_STREAMS - concurrent streams per agent daemon connection
LAYERX_HUMAN_AGENT_MAX_QUEUED_BYTES - bytes queued towards the agent daemon before back-pressure
LAYERX_HUMAN_AGENT_DEADLINE_SECONDS - deadline of one agent daemon exchange in seconds
LAYERX_HUMAN_AGENT_ACTOR - agent DID the human service acts as towards the kernel
LAYERX_HUMAN_AGENT_AUTHORITY - authority reference the human service signs under
LAYERX_HUMAN_AGENT_TIMESTAMP_SPAN_SECONDS - accepted timestamp span of an agent activity in seconds
LAYERX_HUMAN_AGENT_FEE_LIMIT - highest fee the human service authorises on an activity
LAYERX_HUMAN_AGENT_PURPOSE_CATALOG - absolute path of the agent purpose catalog file
LAYERX_HUMAN_AGENT_OWNER_ACCOUNT - kernel account that owns agents created by the service
LAYERX_HUMAN_AGENT_RECOVERY_ROOT - base64url 32-byte root of the agent recovery derivation
LAYERX_HUMAN_AGENT_RECOVERY_THRESHOLD - guardians required to recover an agent
LAYERX_HUMAN_SECURITY_SOCKET - absolute path of the security provider socket
LAYERX_HUMAN_SECURITY_DEADLINE_SECONDS - deadline of one security provider call in seconds
LAYERX_HUMAN_SECURITY_MAX_FRAME_BYTES - largest frame exchanged with the security provider
LAYERX_HUMAN_IDENTITY_SOCKET - absolute path of the identity provider socket
LAYERX_HUMAN_IDENTITY_DEADLINE_SECONDS - deadline of one identity provider call in seconds
LAYERX_HUMAN_IDENTITY_MAX_FRAME_BYTES - largest frame exchanged with the identity provider
LAYERX_HUMAN_IDENTITY_PEER_UID - uid the identity provider socket must present
LAYERX_HUMAN_IDENTITY_PEER_GID - gid the identity provider socket must present
LAYERX_HUMAN_IDENTITY_BINDING_SOCKET - absolute path of the identity binding socket
